a rook, and 19…h5 threatens …hxg4, winning a pawn. Black is two pawns down: Black holds the balance (+0.01). This is White's best try."},{"title":"Why not save the knight first?","text":"Saving it with 16…Nf6, the best way to do that, is clearly weaker (+1.89 against −0.30). White answers 17.Qh6+. That would leave Black clearly worse."}]},{"ply":34,"name":"17…Rc5","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"17…Rc5! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Moving away uncovers the queen on a5, which now hits the queen on d2.","Moves the attacked rook to safety.","The next best move, 17…Rbc8, would drop Black's winning chances from 53% to 19% (+4.01).","17…Rc5 threatens …Rxh5, winning a pawn.","It threatens …Rxh5, winning a pawn, so White has to spend the next move on it.","White answers 18.Qd4+, giving check, leaving Black with a king with pawns missing from its shelter."]},{"ply":150,"name":"75…Bf7","cls":"miss","color":"b","headline":"75…Bf7 misses the chance 75.Kc3 gave: 75…Qxa3 would have punished it. Black's winning chances go from 69% to 53%.","points":["White answers 76.Qd4.","Better was 75…Qxa3 (−2.19), which takes the pawn on a3."],"better":"75…Qxa3 wins a pawn. After 76.Qd4 Be6+ 77.Kd2 Qa2+ 78.Kc1 Bf5, Black comes out a pawn up (−2.19)."},{"ply":172,"name":"86…Bd5","cls":"blunder","color":"b","headline":"86…Bd5 is a blunder: Black's winning chances go from 50% to 6%.","points":["White answers 87.Rxd5, which takes the bishop on d5.","The bishop on d5 can be taken by the rook on a5.","After Rxd5, White wins 3 points of material within 2 moves.","Better was 86…g3 (0.00), which pushes the passed pawn to g3, close to promotion."],"better":"86…g3 pushes the passed pawn to g3. Engine line: 87.a4 Kg4 88.Ra7 Bd5 89.Rd7 Be4 (0.00)."},{"ply":173,"name":"87.Kf2","cls":"miss","color":"w","headline":"87.Kf2 misses 87.Rxd5, which wins material. White's winning chances go from 94% to 74%.","points":["Black answers 87…Be4: plants the bishop on e4: 